@scottshambaugh  I’ve tried a similar setup with uv on my side and it worked pretty smoothly for me as well.

The steps you outlined match what I ended up with, including the editable install with --no-build-isolation, which I’ve found is often needed anyway when working on Matplotlib locally. Using uv run to sanity-check the install is also nice since it avoids depending on whether the environment is activated or not.

I agree that the bigger questions are more around long-term support than whether this works in practice — documenting an alternative workflow and making sure CI covers it would be the heavier lift. As a personal dev setup though, this seems totally reasonable, and it’s useful to have the experience written down here for others who are already using uv.

